1
00:00:18,398 --> 00:00:21,633
So do you think
Nero will try to win her back?

2
00:00:21,634 --> 00:00:23,570
This is exciting.

3
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:25,005
I hope they patch things up

4
00:00:25,005 --> 00:00:27,474
and I hope they'll end up together,

5
00:00:27,474 --> 00:00:29,442
so there'll be a sequel to this story.

6
00:00:29,442 --> 00:00:30,644
Good morning, Florence.

7
00:00:30,644 --> 00:00:33,046
What are you doing here?

8
00:00:33,046 --> 00:00:37,017
Florence, he's been waiting here
for quite some time.

9
00:00:37,017 --> 00:00:39,999
He said you owe him dinner

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:41,434
because in the auction,

11
00:00:41,434 --> 00:00:44,601
he bid a million pesos
for you to cook for him.

12
00:00:44,601 --> 00:00:45,833
Is that true?

13
00:00:45,834 --> 00:00:48,461
Well, I thought
that letting go would be difficult,

14
00:00:48,461 --> 00:00:52,432
but the truth is
I seem to be coping pretty well.

15
00:00:52,432 --> 00:00:53,533
That's good.

16
00:00:53,533 --> 00:00:56,369
You act like I'm the only broken-hearted one.

17
00:00:56,369 --> 00:00:58,137
What about you?

18
00:00:58,838 --> 00:01:01,007
I can't believe that girl.

19
00:01:01,007 --> 00:01:04,911
The audacity to show herself to us
after what she did to Florence.

20
00:01:04,911 --> 00:01:07,981
She's using her charms again to trap Owen.

21
00:01:07,981 --> 00:01:11,584
Lina, girl,
why don't you keep an eye on Owen?

22
00:01:11,584 --> 00:01:14,854
I think you two will be perfect together.

23
00:01:14,854 --> 00:01:16,122
Yes.

24
00:01:16,122 --> 00:01:20,460
What I'm saying is,
do you agree to set me up with Owen?

25
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:22,295
Is it bad?

26
00:01:22,295 --> 00:01:24,464
Is it prohibited?

27
00:01:24,464 --> 00:01:25,932
We don't have a relationship.

28
00:01:25,932 --> 00:01:27,534
You're right.

29
00:01:27,534 --> 00:01:30,170
Maybe I should be dating someone else.

30
00:01:30,170 --> 00:01:33,940
Now, get some mangoes
so we'll have something for dessert later.

31
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,042
Okay, which one?

32
00:01:36,042 --> 00:01:37,711
Is this okay?

33
00:01:37,711 --> 00:01:40,680
No, that's not good. It has patches.
Get the other one.

34
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,816
- This one?
- No, not that one.

35
00:01:42,816 --> 00:01:44,617
The other one.

36
00:01:44,617 --> 00:01:46,418
That one.

37
00:01:48,788 --> 00:01:51,085
Nero!

38
00:01:51,085 --> 00:01:54,828
- Ouch...
- You can't walk with that?

39
00:01:54,828 --> 00:01:55,996
I can.

40
00:01:55,996 --> 00:01:59,032
- Just wait.
- We need to get out of here.

41
00:01:59,032 --> 00:02:01,301
- Ouch.
- Wait.

42
00:02:01,301 --> 00:02:02,235
- Just take it slow.
- Ouch, wait.

43
00:02:02,235 --> 00:02:04,037
We're getting soaked already.

44
00:02:04,037 --> 00:02:06,106
Ouch, wait.

45
00:02:06,106 --> 00:02:08,240
Wait...

46
00:02:57,023 --> 00:02:59,125
There you go.

47
00:02:59,125 --> 00:03:01,294
Are you okay now?

48
00:03:01,294 --> 00:03:03,128
I'm okay now.

49
00:03:03,730 --> 00:03:05,799
Well...

50
00:03:05,799 --> 00:03:07,566
are you okay?

51
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:15,241
Are you asking if Florence and I are okay?

52
00:03:15,241 --> 00:03:18,445
Obviously, you're still at the losing end.

53
00:03:18,445 --> 00:03:22,182
It looks like my only daughter
is still fuming mad at you.

54
00:03:22,182 --> 00:03:24,049
Well, a bit.

55
00:03:24,651 --> 00:03:28,955
I thought we were doing okay earlier,

56
00:03:28,955 --> 00:03:33,226
because we were slowly
going back to what we were before.

57
00:03:33,226 --> 00:03:37,363
But things suddenly changed.

58
00:03:38,264 --> 00:03:40,900
I'm getting a bit confused already.

59
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:45,672
I don't understand if I did something bad
or said something wrong.

60
00:03:45,672 --> 00:03:48,141
What did he do wrong?

61
00:03:48,141 --> 00:03:50,442
Did he say something wrong?

62
00:03:51,511 --> 00:03:53,734
Nothing really, Mother.

63
00:03:53,734 --> 00:03:58,169
The truth is, earlier,
we were starting to be okay,

64
00:03:58,169 --> 00:04:01,354
but for no apparent reason,
I suddenly got annoyed with him.

65
00:04:01,354 --> 00:04:04,057
I suddenly became mad.

66
00:04:04,057 --> 00:04:08,027
Maybe I still haven't forgotten
what he did to me, Mother.

67
00:04:08,027 --> 00:04:10,562
He made me look like a fool.

68
00:04:11,464 --> 00:04:13,532
You know, to tell you the truth...

69
00:04:14,234 --> 00:04:17,737
when I found out
that you broke my daughter's heart,

70
00:04:17,737 --> 00:04:21,206
I wanted to crush you.

71
00:04:21,927 --> 00:04:24,896
But when we saw you earlier...

72
00:04:26,246 --> 00:04:32,252
When you dared to face us,

73
00:04:32,252 --> 00:04:34,219
you humbled yourself.

74
00:04:35,755 --> 00:04:40,759
I said to myself, maybe this guy is okay.

75
00:04:41,628 --> 00:04:44,697
You are still young,
that's why you made a mistake.

76
00:04:46,699 --> 00:04:48,568
It's not that I'm pushing, Florence.

77
00:04:48,568 --> 00:04:52,292
The truth is,
I don't like those boy-girl things.

78
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:56,976
But if you're saying Nero is at fault,

79
00:04:56,976 --> 00:05:00,480
then you're a little wrong.

80
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,081
Mother, why am I at fault?

81
00:05:02,081 --> 00:05:05,118
No, I'm not saying you're at fault.

82
00:05:05,118 --> 00:05:11,457
What I'm saying is,
you should be true to what you're feeling.

83
00:05:11,457 --> 00:05:15,528
The problem with you both
is you became cowards.

84
00:05:15,528 --> 00:05:19,398
You became cowards to say
what you're feeling for each other.

85
00:05:20,066 --> 00:05:22,502
That's how love is.

86
00:05:22,502 --> 00:05:24,804
You should express it.

87
00:05:24,804 --> 00:05:29,442
You should express it in words and actions.

88
00:05:29,442 --> 00:05:30,877
Just like me and my wife.

89
00:05:30,877 --> 00:05:35,080
If only we can say "I love you" every day.

90
00:05:37,383 --> 00:05:41,420
Wait, when was the last time I said
"I love you" to Lydia?

91
00:05:42,322 --> 00:05:44,089
Keep it to yourself.

92
00:05:47,293 --> 00:05:51,931
Florence, the greatest love stories
are the things you talk about.

93
00:05:51,931 --> 00:05:55,168
The ones you write in love letters,

94
00:05:55,168 --> 00:05:58,103
they sometimes become poems.

95
00:05:59,105 --> 00:06:01,741
Let me ask you.

96
00:06:01,741 --> 00:06:06,246
Have you tried to sit in front of Nero,

97
00:06:06,246 --> 00:06:13,552
and stare into his eyes
and tell him what's inside your heart?

98
00:06:20,493 --> 00:06:24,296
Have you told her
everything you feel deep inside?

99
00:06:26,032 --> 00:06:28,067
Were you sincere?

100
00:06:29,669 --> 00:06:32,105
Maybe that's what you need.

101
00:06:32,105 --> 00:06:36,509
You need a chance to talk
sincerely and thoroughly,

102
00:06:36,509 --> 00:06:42,514
so you can fix your misunderstanding.

103
00:06:48,121 --> 00:06:49,789
Lina?

104
00:06:49,789 --> 00:06:52,524
Wait, come on.

105
00:06:54,427 --> 00:06:57,630
Is it true that there's something
between you and Troy?

106
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,932
Oh my God.

107
00:06:59,932 --> 00:07:02,101
This is a surprise.

108
00:07:02,101 --> 00:07:04,037
Are we missing an episode in your life?

109
00:07:04,037 --> 00:07:06,939
Because we're not prepared
for this kind of revelation.

110
00:07:06,939 --> 00:07:09,808
We didn't mean it.

111
00:07:10,543 --> 00:07:17,116
Girl, I've just realized
that you have some secret moves...

112
00:07:17,116 --> 00:07:19,702
In fairness, your moves are so suave.

113
00:07:19,702 --> 00:07:23,382
- Yeah, girl.
- I thought your bullying days are over.

114
00:07:23,382 --> 00:07:25,458
You're picking on me again.

115
00:07:25,458 --> 00:07:29,128
Hey, you're so sensitive.

116
00:07:29,128 --> 00:07:30,963
Yes, can't you take a joke?

117
00:07:30,963 --> 00:07:33,832
Is that why you were
throwing a tantrum earlier?

118
00:07:35,201 --> 00:07:38,938
I'm just annoyed because
should I take the initiative

119
00:07:38,938 --> 00:07:40,973
between the two of us?

120
00:07:41,841 --> 00:07:46,913
Girl, today is all about girl power.

121
00:07:46,913 --> 00:07:52,285
So, if Troy refuses to make a move,
why not you make a move?

122
00:07:52,285 --> 00:07:55,621
This is a queen's gambit era.

123
00:07:55,621 --> 00:07:57,623
Take the initiative.

124
00:07:57,623 --> 00:08:02,161
The powerful queen's opening
until it's checkmate.

125
00:08:02,895 --> 00:08:07,266
Sometimes, I have no idea about
Camille's pop culture reference,

126
00:08:07,266 --> 00:08:08,701
but I totally get her.

127
00:08:08,701 --> 00:08:10,937
- Yeah.
- I totally agree with her.

128
00:08:10,937 --> 00:08:13,005
So what are you waiting for?

129
00:08:13,005 --> 00:08:15,474
What's your opening move?

130
00:08:21,414 --> 00:08:23,552
So what are you afraid of?

131
00:08:23,552 --> 00:08:26,419
If you really like her, go for it.

132
00:08:26,419 --> 00:08:28,254
You're the most talkative among us.

133
00:08:28,254 --> 00:08:29,889
Why are you so quiet all of a sudden?

134
00:08:29,889 --> 00:08:32,357
It's not that easy.

135
00:08:35,428 --> 00:08:37,430
Are you gossiping about me?

136
00:08:37,430 --> 00:08:38,931
No, Grandfather.

137
00:08:38,931 --> 00:08:41,066
It's just girl problems, Grandfather.

138
00:08:41,801 --> 00:08:46,439
And with the look on your faces,
it seems like it's Troy who has a problem.

139
00:08:46,439 --> 00:08:48,975
This is nothing, Grandfather.
Don't worry about me.

140
00:08:48,975 --> 00:08:51,544
I can manage this. I'm okay.

141
00:08:51,544 --> 00:08:53,645
Are you really okay?

142
00:08:55,148 --> 00:08:57,550
I think what you're experiencing right now

143
00:08:57,550 --> 00:09:01,954
is the crippling fear of rejection.

144
00:09:03,856 --> 00:09:05,725
That's what we're all scared of,

145
00:09:05,725 --> 00:09:10,296
to find someone you love dearly,
but doesn't love you.

146
00:09:10,296 --> 00:09:15,273
Will it hurt if you open your heart
and give everything,

147
00:09:15,273 --> 00:09:17,269
and then she doesn't love you?

148
00:09:20,651 --> 00:09:24,210
Of course, it will hurt, very bad!

149
00:09:24,210 --> 00:09:27,180
Ouch, it hurts so much.

150
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:30,383
But it's not the worst thing in the world.

151
00:09:30,383 --> 00:09:34,503
The worst thing in the world is regret.

152
00:09:35,817 --> 00:09:40,221
Going on living not knowing
what could have been.

153
00:09:41,327 --> 00:09:46,199
I'm giving you all these opportunities,
not because I want to spoil you,

154
00:09:46,199 --> 00:09:51,527
but because I want to give you a chance
to find what you really want.

155
00:09:51,527 --> 00:09:54,640
Because I don't want you
to look back in the past,

156
00:09:54,640 --> 00:10:00,045
thinking about what could've been,
or might have been.

157
00:10:00,713 --> 00:10:04,617
My advice... is don't be scared.

158
00:10:04,617 --> 00:10:07,019
Because for every chance of getting hurt,

159
00:10:07,019 --> 00:10:13,258
is also a chance to find happiness
in this life.

160
00:10:14,794 --> 00:10:16,336
Yeah.

161
00:10:23,909 --> 00:10:26,144
What are you cooking?

162
00:10:27,573 --> 00:10:29,441
Adobo.

163
00:10:30,076 --> 00:10:33,117
It seems you've been cooking
for quite some time.

164
00:10:33,117 --> 00:10:36,019
Isn't it easy to cook adobo?

165
00:10:37,305 --> 00:10:39,785
It depends on the adobo.

166
00:10:39,785 --> 00:10:41,387
There are different ways of cooking it.

167
00:10:41,387 --> 00:10:44,357
Just like this,
I didn't cook it in soy sauce.

168
00:10:44,357 --> 00:10:46,246
Just salt and vinegar.

169
00:10:46,246 --> 00:10:50,730
That's why,
you have to be careful in mixing it

170
00:10:50,730 --> 00:10:53,866
until it releases its own oil.

171
00:10:53,866 --> 00:10:58,471
In short, you're cooking the meat
in its own oil,

172
00:10:58,471 --> 00:11:01,841
but you should always keep an eye on it.

173
00:11:01,841 --> 00:11:05,344
Because you might look away
and it'll be overcooked.

174
00:11:05,344 --> 00:11:07,145
It won't be delicious anymore.

175
00:11:12,451 --> 00:11:16,255
There are things that you can't rush...

176
00:11:16,255 --> 00:11:18,724
or force.

177
00:11:18,724 --> 00:11:21,660
Some things need time and space...

178
00:11:22,895 --> 00:11:24,730
just like us.

179
00:11:29,602 --> 00:11:34,706
The reason why I said what I did,
is because I'm protecting you.

180
00:11:36,409 --> 00:11:41,914
But that's an excuse,
because no matter what I do...

181
00:11:41,914 --> 00:11:44,717
I still hurt you.

182
00:11:44,717 --> 00:11:48,688
I'm hurting the person
who my heart really wants.

183
00:11:48,688 --> 00:11:52,090
Maybe I'm the last person you want to see.

184
00:11:53,292 --> 00:11:57,028
This face reminds you
of all the bad feelings.

185
00:11:57,993 --> 00:12:01,162
I should've given you space and time first.

186
00:12:02,234 --> 00:12:04,136
Don't worry...

187
00:12:04,770 --> 00:12:07,840
I will wait, Florence.

188
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,941
I will wait for you.

189
00:12:48,681 --> 00:12:51,750
There are things that you can't rush...

190
00:12:52,618 --> 00:12:54,920
or force.

191
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,989
Some things need time and space...

192
00:12:59,158 --> 00:13:00,926
just like us.

193
00:13:06,165 --> 00:13:11,336
The reason why I said what I did,
is because I'm protecting you.

194
00:13:13,005 --> 00:13:15,741
But that's an excuse,

195
00:13:15,741 --> 00:13:18,611
because no matter what I do...

196
00:13:18,611 --> 00:13:21,280
I still hurt you.

197
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:25,351
I'm hurting the person
who my heart really wants.

198
00:13:25,351 --> 00:13:28,653
Maybe I'm the last person you want to see.

199
00:13:29,822 --> 00:13:33,692
This face reminds you
of all the bad feelings.

200
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:37,829
I should've given you space and time first.

201
00:13:38,864 --> 00:13:40,699
Don't worry.

202
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,735
I will wait, Florence.

203
00:13:44,370 --> 00:13:46,471
I will wait for you.

204
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:02,922
So what now?

205
00:14:02,922 --> 00:14:04,623
He'll just leave as if nothing happened?

206
00:14:04,623 --> 00:14:06,491
Just like that?

207
00:14:29,014 --> 00:14:30,583
Hey!

208
00:14:30,583 --> 00:14:32,118
Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell,

209
00:14:32,118 --> 00:14:35,320
are you really going to leave
as if nothing happened?

210
00:14:47,862 --> 00:14:49,122
What?

211
00:14:49,122 --> 00:14:51,637
You're leaving, that's just it?

212
00:14:51,637 --> 00:14:55,795
I thought
you were not comfortable with my presence.

213
00:14:55,795 --> 00:14:58,930
That's why I'm going to give you some space.

214
00:14:59,598 --> 00:15:01,200
Space?

215
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:04,070
Do I look like a rocket ship to you?

216
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:08,140
Did you even ask me
if that's what I need or that's what I want?

217
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:10,643
That's what I'm saying.
That's the problem with you.

218
00:15:10,643 --> 00:15:12,945
You assume too much.

219
00:15:12,945 --> 00:15:16,315
Hey!
You're from Gyronella, not from Assumption.

220
00:15:16,315 --> 00:15:19,351
You assume too much
about what I want in my life.

221
00:15:19,351 --> 00:15:21,921
And yes, you're right.

222
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:24,757
I'm pissed whenever I see you.
Do you know why?

223
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:27,059
Because I remember what you did to me.

224
00:15:27,059 --> 00:15:28,994
And every time I remember what you did to me,

225
00:15:28,994 --> 00:15:33,231
I want to kick you and crush you
to fine pieces.

226
00:15:37,203 --> 00:15:40,371
But it doesn't mean
that I don't want to see you anymore.

227
00:15:40,372 --> 00:15:41,666
It doesn't mean

228
00:15:41,667 --> 00:15:45,010
that you shouldn't show yourself
and then leave.

229
00:15:45,911 --> 00:15:48,748
And that doesn't mean...

230
00:15:48,748 --> 00:15:51,717
that all my feelings for you
will just go away.

231
00:15:51,717 --> 00:15:53,085
What?

232
00:15:53,085 --> 00:15:55,588
Even if you turn the world upside down,

233
00:15:55,588 --> 00:15:58,657
even if I hit my head there now,

234
00:15:58,657 --> 00:16:02,061
it's still you who my heart wants.

235
00:16:02,061 --> 00:16:03,564
What?

236
00:16:04,830 --> 00:16:06,565
You'll just pretend you don't know?

237
00:16:06,565 --> 00:16:08,267
Don't tell me you didn't hear that clearly.

238
00:16:08,267 --> 00:16:10,136
Are you going
to make me repeat everything, Nero?

239
00:16:10,136 --> 00:16:11,767
I heard everything.

240
00:16:13,172 --> 00:16:15,808
What will you do now?
Will you just stand there? Don't you want it?

241
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:17,710
Of course, I want.

242
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:19,477
I can't hear it.

243
00:16:20,112 --> 00:16:21,847
I like you, Florence.

244
00:16:21,847 --> 00:16:23,072
I can't hear it.

245
00:16:23,072 --> 00:16:25,251
I like you, Florence.

246
00:16:25,251 --> 00:16:26,752
I like you so much!

247
00:16:26,752 --> 00:16:28,420
I like Florence!

248
00:16:28,420 --> 00:16:33,024
Hey, neighbors! Florence has a boyfriend!

249
00:16:34,927 --> 00:16:36,728
I like you.

250
00:16:37,363 --> 00:16:39,598
I like Florence!

251
00:16:49,642 --> 00:16:50,976
Lydia!

252
00:16:50,976 --> 00:16:53,912
- Something is happening outside.
- Huh?

253
00:17:26,011 --> 00:17:28,914
You fools! Why are you tolerating this?

254
00:17:28,914 --> 00:17:31,183
What do you mean kiss?

255
00:17:31,183 --> 00:17:33,152
Nero, Florencia!

256
00:17:33,152 --> 00:17:34,220
Get inside!

257
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:35,588
We're going to eat now.

258
00:17:35,588 --> 00:17:37,690
Get inside.

259
00:17:37,690 --> 00:17:38,691
- Father...
- Get inside!

260
00:17:38,691 --> 00:17:39,658
Mother.

261
00:17:39,658 --> 00:17:41,727
- Mother!
- Okay.

262
00:17:41,727 --> 00:17:43,528
- Kiss, Father...
- Get inside.

263
00:17:44,196 --> 00:17:45,197
- Get inside.
- Father...

264
00:17:45,197 --> 00:17:46,965
I'll kiss you, Mother.

265
00:17:48,655 --> 00:17:50,636
I'm happy with you both

266
00:17:50,636 --> 00:17:53,806
because your feelings for
each other are so connected.

267
00:17:53,806 --> 00:17:59,979
But let me remind you, you're still young.

268
00:17:59,979 --> 00:18:05,216
I will only allow you to have a relationship
if there are rules.

269
00:18:05,951 --> 00:18:08,153
That's right.

270
00:18:08,153 --> 00:18:09,788
Why are you winking?

271
00:18:09,788 --> 00:18:12,924
I'm winking at you because you're sexy.

272
00:18:13,826 --> 00:18:17,997
Don't worry. I respect your wishes.

273
00:18:17,997 --> 00:18:19,899
Very good answer.

274
00:18:19,899 --> 00:18:21,901
First rule.

275
00:18:21,901 --> 00:18:24,336
No kissing.

276
00:18:24,336 --> 00:18:26,272
- What?
- Don't you want that?

277
00:18:26,272 --> 00:18:29,108
No, that's right. Your mother is correct.

278
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:30,799
- She's right.
- Mother.

279
00:18:30,799 --> 00:18:33,812
Nero and I are not thinking about that.

280
00:18:33,812 --> 00:18:36,081
What do mean you're not thinking about it?

281
00:18:36,081 --> 00:18:39,852
Earlier, the neighbors were egging you,
and you're already game.

282
00:18:39,852 --> 00:18:43,121
Your lips were as long as EDSA.

283
00:18:44,523 --> 00:18:46,659
I agree with mother.

284
00:18:46,659 --> 00:18:48,761
Don't be pressured, Florence.

285
00:18:48,761 --> 00:18:49,929
Mother?

286
00:18:49,929 --> 00:18:51,730
You're calling me Mother that soon?

287
00:18:51,730 --> 00:18:53,098
Wow!

288
00:18:53,098 --> 00:18:56,969
Hey, Nero. I trust you.

289
00:18:56,969 --> 00:19:00,605
Don't ruin my trust in you.

290
00:19:02,541 --> 00:19:04,310
Wait, just to be clear.

291
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:06,211
So what's allowed?

292
00:19:06,211 --> 00:19:08,180
Kiss on the cheeks?

293
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:09,949
No, that's not allowed.

294
00:19:09,949 --> 00:19:12,518
That's near the lips.

295
00:19:12,518 --> 00:19:13,819
Kiss on the forehead?

296
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:15,554
Father, what am I?

297
00:19:15,554 --> 00:19:17,455
Nero's grandchild?

298
00:19:20,926 --> 00:19:24,630
How about... holding hands?

299
00:19:24,630 --> 00:19:26,029
Is that allowed?

300
00:19:27,338 --> 00:19:28,873
Okay.

301
00:19:32,037 --> 00:19:33,806
Kiss on the hand?

302
00:19:33,806 --> 00:19:35,374
Is that allowed?

303
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:36,775
No.

304
00:19:36,775 --> 00:19:38,877
You can't kiss

305
00:19:38,877 --> 00:19:42,480
until you're the lead character
in your own movie.

306
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:46,952
Okay, that's enough.

307
00:19:46,952 --> 00:19:48,920
What I know is...

308
00:19:49,655 --> 00:19:57,495
This is a new and beautiful chapter
in our lives.

309
00:19:58,831 --> 00:20:05,037
And we should always celebrate
the new connections...

310
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:07,973
that we're forming in our journey.

311
00:20:07,973 --> 00:20:09,808
So, Nero...

312
00:20:11,243 --> 00:20:13,078
Welcome to the family.

313
00:20:13,078 --> 00:20:14,847
Welcome.

314
00:20:14,847 --> 00:20:18,683
Cheers.

315
00:20:20,953 --> 00:20:22,754
But a kiss is not allowed.

316
00:20:24,124 --> 00:20:26,205
Nothing. Just holding hands.

317
00:20:26,205 --> 00:20:29,661
Holding hands is allowed while walking.

318
00:20:29,661 --> 00:20:31,533
Are you sleepy already?

319
00:20:31,533 --> 00:20:34,766
I don't know if I'd fall asleep tonight.

320
00:20:36,035 --> 00:20:38,504
Don't be too excited.

321
00:20:38,504 --> 00:20:40,842
I should be excited.

322
00:20:40,842 --> 00:20:43,308
And we're on the way to the exciting part.

323
00:20:43,308 --> 00:20:45,236
Hey, you fool.

324
00:20:45,236 --> 00:20:48,547
Maybe you've forgotten my mother's rules.
You made a promise.

325
00:20:48,547 --> 00:20:54,830
Of course, what I mean is
you're officially part of my world.

326
00:20:54,830 --> 00:20:57,300
Wow, before, you were not talking,

327
00:20:57,300 --> 00:21:01,158
but now, you have remarks like that.

328
00:21:01,158 --> 00:21:03,353
Go ahead and sleep.

329
00:21:04,650 --> 00:21:07,861
Don't I get a good night's kiss?

330
00:21:07,861 --> 00:21:09,968
That's not allowed, remember?

331
00:21:09,968 --> 00:21:11,170
It's not allowed face-to-face,

332
00:21:11,170 --> 00:21:14,539
but they didn't say it's not allowed
over the phone.

333
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:19,711
Oh my, you already found loopholes
in the rules.

334
00:21:19,711 --> 00:21:23,582
<i>You know, that's the problem
why the Philippines is not progressing.</i>

335
00:21:23,582 --> 00:21:26,096
<i>You always make an alibi
until you get away with it.</i>

336
00:21:26,096 --> 00:21:29,053
- That's the only thing I'm asking.
- Here it is.

337
00:21:36,562 --> 00:21:37,760
What's that?

338
00:21:37,760 --> 00:21:39,531
That's it.

339
00:21:39,531 --> 00:21:42,834
One more, the signal is a bit choppy.

340
00:21:49,542 --> 00:21:51,263
Thank you.

341
00:21:51,263 --> 00:21:53,579
What do you mean thank you?
Are you saying it's just me?

342
00:21:53,579 --> 00:21:57,516
The business will go bankrupt
if that's how you do it.

343
00:21:57,516 --> 00:21:59,126
It's embarrassing.

344
00:21:59,126 --> 00:22:01,384
Oh, so that's it.

345
00:22:01,384 --> 00:22:04,823
If you do it, it's embarrassing,
but if I do it, it's okay.

346
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:07,325
Okay, I'm just getting ready.

347
00:22:15,611 --> 00:22:17,735
There are no feelings.

348
00:22:22,875 --> 00:22:25,233
Did you close your eyes?

349
00:22:25,233 --> 00:22:27,912
You should close your eyes.
One more time, come on.

350
00:22:32,951 --> 00:22:34,719
One more...

351
00:22:38,056 --> 00:22:40,792
- What's that, 20?
- It's 20.

352
00:22:47,433 --> 00:22:49,816
You're early even though you came home
late last night.

353
00:22:49,816 --> 00:22:51,488
Come on, let's have breakfast.

354
00:22:51,488 --> 00:22:52,973
You cooked, Grandfather?

355
00:22:52,973 --> 00:22:56,144
Well, you know with the attitude
of my grandsons,

356
00:22:56,144 --> 00:23:01,013
no chef stays long with us,
so we just tried to cook.

357
00:23:01,013 --> 00:23:03,749
So there you go. That's the result.

358
00:23:03,749 --> 00:23:05,330
You know, Nero,

359
00:23:05,330 --> 00:23:08,887
even if you don't ask,
your grandfather cooks well.

360
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:13,524
The next thing he'll be cooking is chopsuey.
Right, Grandfather?

361
00:23:16,415 --> 00:23:18,351
Don't do that again.

362
00:23:21,333 --> 00:23:23,167
It's just a joke.

363
00:23:27,339 --> 00:23:33,812
Just a little push and we'll hire you
as a chef to the Ferells.

364
00:23:33,812 --> 00:23:35,948
Quiet!

365
00:23:35,948 --> 00:23:39,604
What?
Come on, sit down and I'll prepare your food.

366
00:23:39,604 --> 00:23:40,906
No need, Ms. Serafica.

367
00:23:40,906 --> 00:23:44,176
I'm going out for brunch,
so it's okay for me to skip breakfast.

368
00:23:44,176 --> 00:23:47,813
But next time, Grandfather,
I'll eat what you've cooked. Promise.

369
00:23:47,813 --> 00:23:50,315
Brunch? We know you'll be with Florence.

370
00:23:50,315 --> 00:23:53,418
Just give her my kisses.

371
00:23:53,418 --> 00:23:56,721
Me too, give her my hugs and kisses.

372
00:23:58,001 --> 00:23:59,936
Me too, Nero.

373
00:24:01,193 --> 00:24:05,196
Of course, don't forget Mr. Dencio...

374
00:24:08,633 --> 00:24:11,536
- Nero! Us too.
- Us too, Nero...

375
00:24:15,854 --> 00:24:17,008
Smoochie-smooch.

376
00:24:17,008 --> 00:24:18,176
Nero left already.

377
00:24:18,176 --> 00:24:19,745
It's not Nero...

378
00:24:19,745 --> 00:24:21,067
Nero.

379
00:24:21,067 --> 00:24:23,915
- Bye, Mother. Bye, Father.
- We'll go ahead.

380
00:24:26,801 --> 00:24:29,103
Are you laughing at me too?

381
00:24:29,103 --> 00:24:30,234
Of course not.

382
00:24:30,234 --> 00:24:31,167
I'm just imagining

383
00:24:31,167 --> 00:24:36,033
Grandfather Garp, Ma'am Serafica, Mr. Dencio,
Mr. Iking, Mr. James, and Ms. Patotina

384
00:24:36,033 --> 00:24:38,400
pranking you.

385
00:24:39,744 --> 00:24:41,712
It's really funny.

386
00:24:41,712 --> 00:24:45,399
But seriously, Grandfather Garp is cooking?

387
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:46,636
Yes.

388
00:24:47,685 --> 00:24:49,633
I pity Grandfather Garp.

389
00:24:49,634 --> 00:24:52,604
If only I was still in the mansion.

390
00:24:52,604 --> 00:24:55,607
You know, it looks like he's enjoying it.

391
00:24:55,607 --> 00:24:57,713
And Ms. Serafica is there.

392
00:24:57,714 --> 00:25:00,299
The truth is, we don't really need a cook,

393
00:25:00,300 --> 00:25:02,636
we just got used to someone's cooking.

394
00:25:02,636 --> 00:25:04,905
And it's okay that grandfather is cooking.

395
00:25:04,905 --> 00:25:07,107
It's like he found a new hobby.

396
00:25:07,107 --> 00:25:08,408
With cooking?

397
00:25:08,408 --> 00:25:09,676
- Yes.
- Really?

398
00:25:09,676 --> 00:25:12,267
Well then,
I'll send him more and more recipes,

399
00:25:12,267 --> 00:25:15,266
especially his favorites and yours too.

400
00:25:15,267 --> 00:25:17,066
That's a good idea.

401
00:25:17,067 --> 00:25:19,900
But wait, Nero,
why did you pick me up this early?

402
00:25:19,901 --> 00:25:21,019
What's happening?

403
00:25:21,019 --> 00:25:23,734
Today is the first day
to the road to happiness.

404
00:25:23,734 --> 00:25:29,106
And I'm planning to celebrate that
with the longest date in history.

405
00:25:29,106 --> 00:25:32,109
Really? The longest date in history?

406
00:25:32,109 --> 00:25:35,313
Yes. And I already have plans for that.

407
00:25:35,313 --> 00:25:39,150
We'll go strolling at the park,
we'll watch a movie,

408
00:25:39,150 --> 00:25:41,919
we'll attend a mass in Baclaran Church...

409
00:25:41,919 --> 00:25:43,855
we'll try the rides in the amusement park,

410
00:25:43,855 --> 00:25:46,190
and we'll do sunset watching.

411
00:25:46,190 --> 00:25:48,600
That's a lot.

412
00:25:48,601 --> 00:25:51,329
That's why it's the longest date in history.

413
00:25:51,329 --> 00:25:53,965
And I've prepared everything.

414
00:25:53,965 --> 00:25:58,566
And the first place we're going,
is to have a delicious brunch.

415
00:25:58,567 --> 00:25:59,537
Brunch?

416
00:25:59,537 --> 00:26:00,771
Yes.

417
00:26:00,771 --> 00:26:02,241
Let's go?

418
00:26:06,665 --> 00:26:08,446
Repeat after me.

419
00:26:08,447 --> 00:26:10,947
Let's go, Florence.

420
00:26:12,047 --> 00:26:14,307
Let's go to the longest date in history.

421
00:26:14,308 --> 00:26:16,109
Wow.

422
00:26:26,697 --> 00:26:28,565
We're here again?

423
00:26:35,139 --> 00:26:37,208
- It's the same waiters again?
- Thank you.

424
00:26:37,208 --> 00:26:39,944
Deja vu.

425
00:26:39,944 --> 00:26:45,249
So, is this the start
of the longest date in history?

426
00:26:45,249 --> 00:26:47,233
This is just the start, Florence.

427
00:26:47,234 --> 00:26:49,770
I still have a lot of surprises for you.

428
00:26:49,770 --> 00:26:51,434
Imagine this.

429
00:26:51,434 --> 00:26:56,841
Before, I only watch dates like this on TV,
and now, I'm having a date too.

430
00:26:56,841 --> 00:27:00,745
And I'll be surprised
because there'll be fireworks all of a sudden!

431
00:27:03,889 --> 00:27:06,517
Am I going to see your fireworks?

432
00:27:06,518 --> 00:27:07,619
Sorry.

433
00:27:07,619 --> 00:27:09,220
Let's pretend I won't be surprised.

434
00:27:09,220 --> 00:27:11,222
There are no fireworks, Florence.

435
00:27:11,222 --> 00:27:16,428
But my surprise is more beautiful
than fireworks.

436
00:27:16,428 --> 00:27:18,563
- More beautiful?
- Yes.

437
00:27:18,563 --> 00:27:20,565
A thousand fireworks?

438
00:27:20,565 --> 00:27:23,015
- Or there are no fireworks?
- There's no fireworks.

439
00:27:23,015 --> 00:27:29,619
Okay, go ahead and order pork adobo,
which is 1,000 pesos per meal,

440
00:27:29,619 --> 00:27:35,212
and the soup, which is 450 pesos
with gold dust ingredients.

441
00:27:37,182 --> 00:27:39,084
But let's share, okay?

442
00:27:39,084 --> 00:27:40,985
It's really expensive.

443
00:27:41,786 --> 00:27:43,722
- You said it.
- As long as we share it.

444
00:27:43,722 --> 00:27:45,023
- Let's share.
- Yes, share.

445
00:27:45,023 --> 00:27:45,957
- Let's share.
- That's it.

446
00:27:45,957 --> 00:27:47,292
That's all.

447
00:27:47,292 --> 00:27:51,329
Excuse me, I'm so sorry to intrude,

448
00:27:51,329 --> 00:27:54,866
but can I talk to Florence
for a couple of minutes?

449
00:27:54,866 --> 00:27:56,768
What are we going to talk about?

450
00:27:56,768 --> 00:27:58,281
Let's go.

451
00:28:09,069 --> 00:28:11,265
I've been meaning to call you,

452
00:28:11,265 --> 00:28:16,336
but I felt
that I should talk to you in person.

453
00:28:17,105 --> 00:28:20,659
Maybe Nero told you already...

454
00:28:20,659 --> 00:28:24,395
but I just wanted to apologize
for my behavior.

455
00:28:26,925 --> 00:28:30,098
I'm sorry, but...

456
00:28:30,098 --> 00:28:33,401
I can't forgive you for what you've done.

457
00:28:42,208 --> 00:28:43,975
I understand.

458
00:28:45,851 --> 00:28:48,486
No, I'm just joking.

459
00:28:48,486 --> 00:28:52,123
Hey, can't you take a joke?
You're so serious.

460
00:28:52,123 --> 00:28:55,801
That's okay, I already get it.

461
00:28:55,801 --> 00:29:00,136
And my boyfriend can make you
do crazy things.

462
00:29:00,136 --> 00:29:04,605
In fairness to you,
you have a fighting spirit,

463
00:29:04,605 --> 00:29:09,009
but it's still wrong
that you resorted to blackmail.

464
00:29:10,275 --> 00:29:14,312
But it's still an A for effort.

465
00:29:14,312 --> 00:29:16,101
Thank you, Florence.

466
00:29:16,101 --> 00:29:19,838
You know what, the way that I see it,

467
00:29:19,838 --> 00:29:24,609
it's Nero who won the jackpot
in your relationship.

468
00:29:24,609 --> 00:29:29,280
And the way that you call him boyfriend
really has a nice ring to it.

469
00:29:29,280 --> 00:29:33,685
Isn't it awkward to call him boyfriend?

470
00:29:33,685 --> 00:29:35,686
It's my first time.

471
00:29:36,421 --> 00:29:38,690
You're awesome, Florence.

472
00:29:38,690 --> 00:29:44,395
And truly,
I sincerely wish you and Nero happiness.

473
00:29:56,508 --> 00:29:58,642
- Sorry, Nero.
- Thank you.

474
00:29:59,244 --> 00:30:00,512
That's okay.

475
00:30:00,512 --> 00:30:02,680
You also need closure.

476
00:30:04,115 --> 00:30:06,151
Exactly.

477
00:30:06,151 --> 00:30:10,288
If you compare it to
the continuation of a drama series,

478
00:30:10,288 --> 00:30:11,637
that's it.

479
00:30:12,489 --> 00:30:14,893
So, let's eat.

480
00:30:14,893 --> 00:30:16,434
Let's dig in.

481
00:30:18,096 --> 00:30:20,231
Florence!

482
00:30:20,231 --> 00:30:24,402
So, the reason why you left early
is that you have a date.

483
00:30:24,402 --> 00:30:27,505
And I knew it, I'll see you here.

484
00:30:27,505 --> 00:30:32,477
I miss you, but I really need you.

485
00:30:32,477 --> 00:30:34,212
I need your advice, Florence.

486
00:30:34,212 --> 00:30:36,047
Advice?

487
00:30:36,047 --> 00:30:37,622
For what?

488
00:30:46,191 --> 00:30:48,593
I got scared, Florence.

489
00:30:48,593 --> 00:30:52,864
Because it was you
who built my persona in the chat.

490
00:30:52,864 --> 00:30:57,013
Now that I've met her in person,
it seems I've lost my confidence.

491
00:30:58,203 --> 00:31:02,278
I can't stop thinking
that she might think I'm a fake,

492
00:31:02,278 --> 00:31:07,011
or worse, that I'm just interesting online
but very boring in real life.

493
00:31:07,011 --> 00:31:09,914
Troy, just relax.

494
00:31:09,914 --> 00:31:12,317
We're talking about Lina.

495
00:31:12,317 --> 00:31:14,953
And if there's one thing I know about Lina,

496
00:31:14,953 --> 00:31:16,967
she won't judge you.

497
00:31:16,968 --> 00:31:18,933
I'm sure

498
00:31:18,934 --> 00:31:22,900
she'll like
both your exciting and boring parts.

499
00:31:22,901 --> 00:31:27,800
And also, your corny side, always.

500
00:31:27,801 --> 00:31:28,767
Really?

501
00:31:28,767 --> 00:31:30,692
Yes, mark my word.

502
00:31:37,364 --> 00:31:39,970
Do you still need anything?

503
00:31:40,968 --> 00:31:43,670
- I feel better.
- You feel better already?

504
00:31:44,582 --> 00:31:47,051
- You're done?
- Thank you.

505
00:31:47,051 --> 00:31:49,186
Thank you.

506
00:31:52,513 --> 00:31:56,239
I'm sorry, Nero,
there are a lot of commercial breaks.

507
00:31:56,247 --> 00:31:58,498
What are we talking about earlier?

508
00:32:00,098 --> 00:32:01,460
Soup?

509
00:32:01,460 --> 00:32:03,695
I'll start eating the soup.

510
00:32:06,805 --> 00:32:08,671
Florence!

511
00:32:19,810 --> 00:32:23,533
What will I do, Florence?

512
00:32:23,534 --> 00:32:26,155
I keep thinking of him...

513
00:32:26,155 --> 00:32:30,061
but ever since he found out it was me,

514
00:32:30,061 --> 00:32:33,097
he's ignoring me and refused to talk to me.

515
00:32:33,097 --> 00:32:37,802
It's like he's a different person.

516
00:32:37,802 --> 00:32:42,239
Or maybe he doesn't find me interesting
in real life?

517
00:32:42,941 --> 00:32:46,267
Maybe I'm more interesting online?

518
00:32:48,046 --> 00:32:52,822
Lina, don't overthink too much.

519
00:32:52,822 --> 00:32:56,197
Maybe he is just waiting
for the right timing.

520
00:32:56,978 --> 00:32:58,857
Really?

521
00:32:58,857 --> 00:33:01,993
I was able to spend a long time
with the Ferells in the mansion.

522
00:33:01,993 --> 00:33:08,366
I became their cook,
that's why I know how they think and move.

523
00:33:08,366 --> 00:33:11,669
And if there's one thing I'm sure about Troy,

524
00:33:11,669 --> 00:33:14,872
he will find you very likable.

525
00:33:16,307 --> 00:33:19,471
I think you're just saying that.

526
00:33:19,471 --> 00:33:26,581
Lina, I am many things,
but you know me, I'm not a liar.

527
00:33:27,518 --> 00:33:29,921
Well, you're right.

528
00:33:29,921 --> 00:33:31,990
So just be patient.

529
00:33:31,990 --> 00:33:34,686
What you're waiting for will come.

530
00:33:34,686 --> 00:33:39,527
But if you can no longer wait,
then take the initiative.

531
00:33:39,527 --> 00:33:41,652
Knock on his heart.

532
00:33:41,652 --> 00:33:45,103
That's what Aira and Camille said.

533
00:33:45,103 --> 00:33:46,532
You can do it.

534
00:33:46,532 --> 00:33:48,742
Just believe in yourself.

535
00:33:50,341 --> 00:33:53,672
I'm so happy I was able to talk to you.

536
00:33:56,381 --> 00:33:58,783
Just knock...

537
00:33:58,783 --> 00:34:00,278
Troy...

538
00:34:00,278 --> 00:34:01,975
Just knock.

539
00:34:01,975 --> 00:34:03,395
You can do it.

540
00:34:08,653 --> 00:34:12,523
Maybe no one will come anymore.

541
00:34:12,523 --> 00:34:15,054
It's too much if someone else arrives.

542
00:34:15,953 --> 00:34:18,312
Let's ask them to reheat the food.

543
00:34:19,470 --> 00:34:21,882
We had them reheat this twice.

544
00:34:23,074 --> 00:34:24,575
Twice?

545
00:34:24,575 --> 00:34:26,156
Twice.

546
00:34:28,246 --> 00:34:29,847
It's still hot.

547
00:34:29,847 --> 00:34:30,982
Let's eat!

548
00:34:30,982 --> 00:34:33,679
So, what were we talking about?

549
00:34:35,267 --> 00:34:37,578
Soup?

550
00:34:42,427 --> 00:34:46,172
Florence Dela Cruz is back!

551
00:34:57,529 --> 00:34:59,186
Yes.

552
00:35:00,545 --> 00:35:03,389
Is there anything else we can do?

553
00:35:05,748 --> 00:35:07,951
Please?

554
00:35:07,951 --> 00:35:10,740
Even if I double the payment?

555
00:35:15,213 --> 00:35:17,081
Okay, fine.

556
00:35:17,081 --> 00:35:18,943
Okay, thank you.

557
00:35:37,428 --> 00:35:39,654
I'm sorry, Nero.

558
00:35:42,773 --> 00:35:44,397
Are you okay?

559
00:35:45,176 --> 00:35:46,701
It's okay.

560
00:35:59,092 --> 00:36:01,846
Let's eat, and then let's go.

561
00:36:01,846 --> 00:36:06,717
Let's carry out your plans
for the longest date in history.

562
00:36:10,889 --> 00:36:14,475
All my reservations were canceled already.

563
00:36:15,593 --> 00:36:18,373
I'm really sorry, Nero.

564
00:36:18,373 --> 00:36:21,709
No, it's okay.

565
00:36:23,834 --> 00:36:26,828
What's important is I was able to be with

566
00:36:26,828 --> 00:36:30,397
the most important person in my life today.

567
00:36:43,621 --> 00:36:49,127
Mr. Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell,

568
00:36:49,127 --> 00:36:53,788
I'd like to thank you for showing me
how big my world is.

569
00:36:56,267 --> 00:36:58,503
Don't be sad anymore.

570
00:36:58,503 --> 00:37:00,166
Go ahead and smile.

571
00:37:03,167 --> 00:37:04,599
Come on, smile...

572
00:37:05,877 --> 00:37:11,131
Smile... Smile.

573
00:37:27,908 --> 00:37:29,429
I know...

574
00:37:35,606 --> 00:37:36,674
What's that?

575
00:37:36,674 --> 00:37:38,273
Copy it.

576
00:37:39,744 --> 00:37:41,429
I don't want to.

577
00:37:41,429 --> 00:37:43,514
Come on, copy it.

578
00:37:43,514 --> 00:37:45,093
Please?

579
00:37:46,751 --> 00:37:48,789
You can do it.

580
00:37:50,171 --> 00:37:51,756
Here.

581
00:37:51,756 --> 00:37:53,468
And stick it...

582
00:37:54,859 --> 00:37:56,523
Stick it.

583
00:38:03,401 --> 00:38:08,797
Mr. Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell...

584
00:38:12,810 --> 00:38:14,969
I love you.

585
00:38:16,314 --> 00:38:20,315
I love you so much.

586
00:38:29,287 --> 00:38:36,800
Ms. Florence Dela Cruz,
I love you so much too.

587
00:38:43,307 --> 00:38:45,298
I love you.

588
00:39:05,763 --> 00:39:08,366
Thank you for today, Nero.

589
00:39:08,366 --> 00:39:11,102
I'm the one who should thank you.

590
00:39:11,102 --> 00:39:14,739
And I can't wait to spend a new day with you.

591
00:39:14,739 --> 00:39:17,241
Oh, go to sleep now.

592
00:39:17,241 --> 00:39:18,976
Good night, my love.

593
00:39:18,976 --> 00:39:21,267
Good night, Love.

594
00:39:26,517 --> 00:39:28,719
Hello?

595
00:39:28,719 --> 00:39:30,913
I thought it's good night already,

596
00:39:30,913 --> 00:39:33,025
why haven't you hung up?

597
00:39:33,025 --> 00:39:34,798
Why haven't you hung up too?

598
00:39:35,726 --> 00:39:37,194
Go ahead and end the call.

599
00:39:37,194 --> 00:39:38,429
You go first.

600
00:39:38,429 --> 00:39:39,697
Okay.

601
00:39:39,697 --> 00:39:42,366
Good night, sweet dreams.

602
00:39:42,366 --> 00:39:43,968
Good night, Nero.

603
00:39:43,968 --> 00:39:46,079
Sweet dreams too.

604
00:39:52,643 --> 00:39:54,312
Hello?

605
00:39:54,312 --> 00:39:55,884
Hey, why are you still there?

606
00:39:55,884 --> 00:39:57,081
End the call.

607
00:39:57,081 --> 00:39:58,883
You go first.

608
00:40:00,284 --> 00:40:02,476
End the call.

609
00:40:03,808 --> 00:40:08,492
Okay, I'll end the call now,
but tomorrow, it's your turn.

610
00:40:08,492 --> 00:40:09,836
Deal.

611
00:40:11,128 --> 00:40:14,719
Hey, Florencia, end that call.
You and Nero should go to sleep!

612
00:40:22,374 --> 00:40:23,710
Hello?

613
00:40:24,589 --> 00:40:27,359
Florencia, go to sleep!

614
00:40:30,616 --> 00:40:33,451
Why is this happening to me?

615
00:40:33,451 --> 00:40:35,619
I was doing okay.

616
00:40:35,619 --> 00:40:39,323
I'm happy with my life
with my mother and father.

617
00:40:39,323 --> 00:40:42,376
I don't need this complication.

618
00:40:42,376 --> 00:40:44,695
Did I do something wrong?

619
00:40:44,695 --> 00:40:47,887
Did I do something bad
for all this to happen to me?

620
00:40:47,887 --> 00:40:51,401
I noticed the first time I saw Florence

621
00:40:51,401 --> 00:40:53,489
that she looks kind of familiar.

622
00:40:53,489 --> 00:40:56,981
Her parents, Lydia and Federico,

623
00:40:56,981 --> 00:40:59,489
they're in a lot of trouble.

624
00:40:59,489 --> 00:41:03,175
Most likely they'll be accused
that they had something to do

625
00:41:03,175 --> 00:41:04,723
with the death of Alyanna Almero.

626
00:41:04,723 --> 00:41:07,262
What happened? What was their reaction?

627
00:41:07,262 --> 00:41:09,239
Denial.

628
00:41:09,239 --> 00:41:12,942
Looking desperate in their attempt
to stand by their lies.

629
00:41:12,942 --> 00:41:13,834
Look, for all I know,

630
00:41:13,834 --> 00:41:17,534
her fake parents are packing their things now
to take my daughter away.

631
00:41:17,534 --> 00:41:19,778
They can't hide.

632
00:41:19,778 --> 00:41:25,313
I will personally look for her
and drag her back here.
